# SAFETY LOCKDOWN — read before touching this file.
#
# This git repository's root ended up being C:\Users\User (your whole
# home directory) instead of C:\Users\User\ClaimDesk. That's a mistake
# from early on, not something worth a risky history rewrite to fix
# right now — but left alone, a single `git add -A` or `git add .` run
# anywhere in this repo would stage every other project, every .env
# file, every credential on this machine for a push to
# github.com/Beezwing/ClaimDesk.
#
# This file closes that hole: everything is ignored by default, and
# only the paths this repo has always legitimately tracked are allowed
# back in. Already-tracked files keep working normally (ignore rules
# never hide or untrack something git already knows about) — this only
# stops NEW, unrelated files from ever being picked up by a broad `add`.
#
# ClaimDesk itself lives right here at the repo root (index.html, src/,
# public/, netlify/, package.json, etc.) — a stale duplicate copy that
# used to sit in a ClaimDesk/ subfolder was removed 2026-09-17.
#
# Adding a new file to ClaimDesk itself? Add its path below.
# Anything else does not belong in this repository.

/*

!/.gitignore
!/.env.example
!/README.md
!/eslint.config.js
!/firestore.rules
!/index.html
!/netlify.toml
!/package.json
!/package-lock.json
!/vite.config.js

!/netlify/
!/public/
!/src/
!/PocketwiseServer/

!/.claude/
/.claude/*
!/.claude/launch.json
